From: Meerzulee / Linux psX maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] usb: xhci-aeolia: select the existing Baikal HDD PHY helper

Adapt the Baikal-only shared-HDD caller from rmuxnet's GPLv2 source at
858d97a4519d4e0110e4b5114b3206ecf05f28d6 (drivers/usb/host/xhci-aeolia.c).
The existing legacy PHY branch stays active for non-Baikal devices. Keep the
existing helper implementation, DMA, IRQ, link, NCQ and delay policy intact.

The helper can defer or fail before an ATA host exists. Propagate only Baikal
pre-host AHCI initialization errors through IRQ/device cleanup before any HCD
is created. This path bypasses remove_hcds, whose idx is uninitialized there.
Preserve post-host error behavior: inherited libata devres callbacks read
drvdata, which this custom driver has restored to axhci rather than ata_host.
Do not newly enter driver-core unwind for that separate lifetime limitation.
Other southbridges retain their existing AHCI-error behavior.

Retain opt-in diagnostics and give the Baikal call distinct begin/end markers
including its return code. A zero return is not proof of PHY readiness: the
existing helper does not propagate its final poll result. This is an
experimental Linux 7.2.11 candidate, with no hardware acceptance.

Original source notices and GPLv2 terms remain unchanged. See BASELINE.json
for immutable source identity and adaptation provenance.

---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-aeolia.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-aeolia.c
